@startuml
title Does this field change when the program moves?
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:A field the assembler emitted;
if (Does it hold a value computed\nfrom labels of the program?) then (no: opcode, #constant, EQU number)
  :Absolute. Never changes.;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
switch (Net relocation of the expression\n+1 per relative name added\n−1 per relative name subtracted)
case (0)
  :A distance, e.g. WORD PTR-VALUE.\nNever changes.;
  stop
case (other)
  :Error: cannot be relocated\n(e.g. VALUE+PTR is net 2).;
  stop
case (1)
endswitch
switch (What kind of field?)
case (format 4 address\nor WORD)
  :Relative. The assembler writes an\nM record; the loader adds the\nload address.;
  stop
case (format 3 PC- or\nbase-relative,\nrelative target)
  :A distance inside the program.\nNever changes.;
  stop
case (format 3 direct, SIC 15-bit,\nPC-relative to an\nabsolute target)
  :Fixed field. Right only where it\nwas assembled; the loader refuses\nto move it.;
  stop
endswitch
@enduml
